Can someone verify how much coded data NH3.0 contains?  Is it something on
the order of 200k+?  The reason I ask is because of the 64k total data
limit on the Turbo C huge model.  This may be a very, very silly question,
but would it be possible (and feasible) to take a huge chunk of that
hard-coded data (monster data, object data, etc) and dump it to data
files, and then have the program _read_ them in _dynamically_?  Would this
free up enough space so that the program could be compiled under the LARGE
model instead?   It seems to me that if the code could be compiled under
this model, it would solve a whole lot of peoples' problems.

Just a thought ... any comments?

